\\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-3{t}^{3})\\cdot 14t\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3t)\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =42{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t-0 \\\\  & =42[\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =42\\left(\\frac{1^{5}}{5}-\\frac{(-1)^{5}}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =42\\left(\\frac{1}{5}-\\left(-\\frac{1}{5}\\right)\\right) \\\\  & =42\\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{84}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540299 1080 "36 \\pi" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540299 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540299 1083 #uuid "86844522-ff99-5a89-bd9a-bb2ab32a4d4c" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540300 1080 "30 \\pi" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540300 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540300 1083 #uuid "87ae3b3a-947a-5634-ba17-7b4b33735361" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540301 1068 #edb/ref 17592186540305 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540301 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540301 1071 "Use Green's theorem to find the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as $r(t)=2\\cos t\\,i+7\\sin t\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,2\\pi].$\n\n![](images/92/92ce9f04a78465f03756605514aab3c48396c66eb8863f16a64b563a8cace6ee.png)" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540301 1072 #uuid "927aab7c-38ca-5938-9f5e-f646a0bd4394" 13194139535909 17592186045443 true] [17592186540301 1074 "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$\n\nOur simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented, and\n\n$$\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=0-(-1)=1.$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D)&=\\iint_D\\text{d}A\\\\&=\\iint_D(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y})\\,\\text{d}A\\\\&=\\oint_C P\\,\\tex